    description: "FOUND 2026-10-21 closing WI-sogof (PR #1796). _choose_init ranks admitted inits by exact-vs-defaulted binding, then by position. swift-composable-architecture's Reduce has init(internal reduce: @escaping (...)) and public init(_ reduce: @escaping (...)); both admit a trailing closure, so 458 'Reduce { state, action in ... }' calls are an ambiguous choice and land on the FIRST by position -- the internal init, which a caller in another module (every test target, every app) cannot see. Fix shape: when the caller's file is outside the init's module (Swift target), drop inits without public/open/package visibility from the admitted tier before ranking; needs the target of a file (Package.swift targets or the Sources/<Target>/ layout). Repro: analyze_swift on TCA, count calls edges into Reduce.init at its init(internal:) span with meta.resolution_quality=ambiguous (458 on the 2026-10-21 census)."  # 54cd
    fields: {}  # 54cd
